74
00:05:00,741 --> 00:05:03,309
Myth: you can use dish soap to wash your
car.

75
00:05:03,659 --> 00:05:08,027
Truth: dish soap strips protective wax and
can dull the paint over time.

76
00:05:08,377 --> 00:05:12,217
Always use a pH‑neutral car shampoo
designed for automotive finishes.

77
00:05:12,566 --> 00:05:13,622
Myth busted.

78
00:05:13,972 --> 00:05:17,356
Myth two: you can wax a ceramic coated car
with any wax.

79
00:05:17,706 --> 00:05:22,170
Truth: only use ceramic‑safe, SiO2‑based
maintenance products.

80
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:24,656
Regular car wax can degrade the coating.

81
00:05:25,006 --> 00:05:28,774
Myth three: a quick detailer spray
replaces a proper wash.

82
00:05:29,124 --> 00:05:33,444
Truth: detailers are for touch‑ups, not
for removing bonded contaminants.

83
00:05:33,794 --> 00:05:37,394
Always do a full wash with pH‑neutral
shampoo first.

84
00:05:37,744 --> 00:05:40,552
Myth four: you don't need to dry the car
after washing.

85
00:05:40,901 --> 00:05:45,533
Truth: water spots can etch the coating,
so dry with a clean microfiber.

86
00:05:45,883 --> 00:05:46,771
Myth busted.

